{
  "schema": "aecp-command-table/1",
  "about": [
    "SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Kebag Logic",
    "SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-W-2.0",
    "The AECP command model (issue #73, REQ-VER-002): one row per command KL_aecp_engine serves.",
    "gen_ucode.py takes its status codes and the MVU command_type from this file, and refuses an entry it never placed.",
    "docs/architecture/06_aecp_engine.md F06.14 is generated from it: python3 scripts/check_aecp_commands.py --write.",
    "scripts/check_aecp_commands.py (make check) holds every other consumer to it: what the engine decodes and dispatches as tb/aecp_cmds observes it (tb/aecp_cmds/decode.json: the programs per opcode, the shortest accepted command, the responses, the GET_DYNAMIC_INFO members and record lengths, the unsolicited jobs), the engine's OP_*_C, GDI_*_C and UPC_*_C values, the top's hazard classifier, the scoreboard's lock-protected classes, the notify block's class map, ucpu_pkg's status codes, the generated ROM's programs and 06 section 8.1.",
    "Sizes are control_data_length (cdl), the offset-from-@12 length; the AECPDU is 12 + cdl octets.",
    "entries are every uPC program the engine dispatches the command to, on any outcome (E_<entry> in gen_ucode.py, UPC_<entry>_C in the engine), the success program first; tb/aecp_cmds observes them.",
    "status is the command's own status set; common_status lists what every command of a message type can also answer."
  ],
  "fields": "aecp_fields.json",
  "status_codes": {
    "SUCCESS": {"code": 0, "rtl": "ST_SUCCESS_C"},
    "NOT_IMPLEMENTED": {"code": 1, "rtl": "ST_NOT_IMPLEMENTED_C"},
    "NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR": {"code": 2, "rtl": "ST_NO_SUCH_DESC_C"},
    "ENTITY_LOCKED": {"code": 3, "rtl": "ST_LOCKED_C"},
    "BAD_ARGUMENTS": {"code": 7, "rtl": "ST_BAD_ARGUMENTS_C"},
    "NO_RESOURCES": {"code": 8, "rtl": "ST_NO_RESOURCES_C"},
    "ENTITY_MISBEHAVING": {"code": 10, "rtl": "ST_ENTITY_MISBEHAVING_C"},
    "NOT_SUPPORTED": {"code": 11, "rtl": "ST_NOT_SUPPORTED_C"},
    "STREAM_IS_RUNNING": {"code": 12, "rtl": null}
  },
  "common_status": {
    "AEM": ["ENTITY_MISBEHAVING"],
    "MVU": ["NOT_IMPLEMENTED"]
  },
  "hazard_classes": {
    "RO_SNAPSHOT": 0,
    "CFG_BARRIER": 1,
    "STREAM_CFG": 2,
    "MAP_CFG": 3,
    "CLOCK_CFG": 4,
    "NAME_WR": 5,
    "LOCK_OP": 6,
    "REGISTRY_OP": 7,
    "IDENTIFY": 8
  },
  "unserved": "NOTIMPL",
  "echo_entries": ["NOTIMPL", "BADARG", "NSUPPE"],
  "shared_entries": {
    "BADARG": "the shared BAD_ARGUMENTS echo; also the first entry of IDENTIFY_NOTIFICATION and the engine-built GET_DYNAMIC_INFO aggregate",
    "NSUPPE": "the shared NOT_SUPPORTED echo; also the first entry of ACQUIRE_ENTITY, which never succeeds",
    "DLKILL": "the deadline kill's arm (03 section 6 rule (e)): every AEM command's ENTITY_MISBEHAVING",
    "NOTIMPL": "the NOT_IMPLEMENTED echo of every command the engine does not serve, on every message type",
    "NOSEND": "an unsolicited job whose kind has no program: retired without a frame",
    "NAMEERR": "the GET_NAME and SET_NAME error body: the engine declares UPC_NAMEERR_C and never dispatches to it; both programs branch there"
  },
